    "notes": "Real kitty scene: gossip whispered over a Housie game. The chip is a loading bar that climbs every shot, so a muted viewer always knows the stake (will we hear it?). Interruptions go ordinary (a number she wins herself, claim first: 'Mera! Mera!'), ordinary (chai, which she then savours while Myra begs), absurd (the cage spun over the key word). Overlapping replies at gap 0.03-0.04. Twist is a see-it person in the door. Button flips the opening: the whisper behind Tina's back becomes Myra asking Tina to her face, and Tanya's 'Baais! Do do baais!' returns as a fake-busy cover. Rewrote once: first ending revealed the gossip (Tina bought a car), which killed the Part 2 hook; second ending had Ruhi tell Tina the story, weaker than the new girl blurting it. Kind humour: the gossip is never said, nobody is mocked."
